      "confidence": 0.95,
      "file_path": "internal/api/handler.go",
      "line_number": 34,
      "line_end": 35,
      "title": "Search query built from request input",
      "description": "Search pastes the name query parameter into the SQL text with fmt.Sprintf. A quote in name ends the string literal and lets the caller append arbitrary SQL. Any caller of GET /users can read or change every row in the database. Use a placeholder in the query and pass name to QueryContext as a bound argument.",
      "suggested_change": "rows, err := h.DB.QueryContext(r.Context(), \"SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE name = ?\", name)",
      "source": "semgrep:go.lang.security.injection.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "Search pastes the name query parameter into the SQL text with fmt.Sprintf. A quote in name ends the string literal and lets the caller append arbitrary SQL.",
      "consequence": "Any caller of GET /users can read or change every row in the database.",
      "fix": "Use a placeholder in the query and pass name to QueryContext as a bound argument."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "critical",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "file_path": "internal/api/handler.go",
      "line_number": 60,
      "line_end": 63,
      "title": "Mutex left locked on missing key",
      "description": "Count locks h.mu before it checks the key. It then returns on an empty key without unlocking. One request to GET /count without a key blocks every later Count request forever. Each blocked request also leaks a goroutine. Validate the key before calling h.mu.Lock. Another option is to call defer h.mu.Unlock right after the lock.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": "semgrep:trailofbits.go.missing-unlock-before-return.missing-unlock-before-return",
      "candidate": "c2",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "Count locks h.mu before it checks the key. It then returns on an empty key without unlocking.",
      "consequence": "One request to GET /count without a key blocks every later Count request forever. Each blocked request also leaks a goroutine.",
      "fix": "Validate the key before calling h.mu.Lock. Another option is to call defer h.mu.Unlock right after the lock."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "file_path": "internal/api/handler.go",
      "line_number": 83,
      "line_end": 86,
      "title": "Response body closed before error check",
      "description": "fetchStatus defers resp.Body.Close before it checks err. When http.Get fails, resp is nil, so the deferred call panics. An unreachable upstream makes GET /upstream panic and drop the connection. The client never gets the intended 502 response. Check err first and return on failure. Defer resp.Body.Close only after that check.",
      "suggested_change": "\tresp, err := http.Get(url)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, err\n\t}\n\tdefer resp.Body.Close()",
      "source": null,
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "fetchStatus defers resp.Body.Close before it checks err. When http.Get fails, resp is nil, so the deferred call panics.",
      "consequence": "An unreachable upstream makes GET /upstream panic and drop the connection. The client never gets the intended 502 response.",
      "fix": "Check err first and return on failure. Defer resp.Body.Close only after that check."
    },
